    description: "INV-zuhub item 1, edge-type family 'calls'. 10+ linkers emit calls edges. The largest family — likely the highest item 1 effort. Audit each for short-name fallback patterns.\n\nLinkers in scope (grep packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/ for 'edge_type=\"calls\"'): cgo, build_target, graphql, grpc, http, ipc, jni, napi, lua_ffi, method_call_recovery, plus others.\n\nKnown concrete violation from the INV-zuhub description: Go interface_dispatch residual cases the WI-jopar receiver-type guard doesn't cover (r.Close() / req.Header.Set(...) resolving to project-internal Alerts.Close/Set per UAT round 02 / DQ-2). See WI-likab discuss-note.\n\nmethod_call_recovery.py is a clear fallback-emit candidate by name — AST-based method-call resolution with collision potential. cgo/jni/napi/lua_ffi may also have C-symbol-name collisions across packages (the Notifier-collision shape from the Apr 2026 Go investigation).\n\nFor each fallback-emitting linker: thread is_fallback through resolver, set conf<=0.5 + meta[disambiguation_fallback]=True at edge-creation, add three property tests. Recommended to start with method_call_recovery.py (highest expected ROI) then work down the list.\n\nParent: INV-zuhub. Pre-condition: commit dd2a93550e."  # e9b8
